 "note": "The Hermitage on the 1901 census - one household of seven - read from the enumerator's page and checked by A. Hagues.\n\n**It is filed at The Hermitage (#392).** The enumerator headed the schedule \"The Hermitage (The Park)\", and the record holds exactly one house of that name, on Hermitage Walk. The household is Sarah Leavers, a widow of 76 born at Derby, a visitor of 72 from Kettering, and five servants - a butler, a cook, two housemaids and a kitchenmaid.\n\nA household kept at that scale by a widow living alone is the kind of establishment that fixes a house, and it bears on [[hermitage-position]], where the building's position in the record is still approximate.",
